Cell["\<\
Non commutative field elements are denoted by the same letter as the \
orthonormal basis elements. Input shortcuts, however, are distinct. Basis \
elements can be input by typing single letter e, (which is immediately \
converted to double struck \[DoubleStruckE] \
(\\[\[VeryThinSpace]DoubleStruckE] ). Noncommutative field elements are input \
by typing double letter ee, which the is automatically converted to double \
struck \[DoubleStruckF]  ( first letter of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]field\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]). Of course one can input them by typing \
corresponding as double struck letters as well. Examples\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.954599430847682*^9, 3.9545994368102837`*^9}, {
  3.954599627098667*^9, 3.9545996310900583`*^9}, {3.9580235943695173`*^9, 
